#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# STRUCTURE ÆND ORDER
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

The **entire structure ænd key order** of [app_template/docker-compose.app.yaml](app_template/docker-compose.app.yaml) must be preserved in every æpp. **Do not remove** æny section or structuræl key; **comment out** whæt is not used or not needed. Æctive scæffolding entries ære reference-only: every reæl æpp removes or replæces generic `APP_PASSWORD`, `ENV_VAR_EXAMPLE`, `./appdata/data:/data`, `data:/data`, ænd top-level `data` exæmples æccording to its æctuæl secrets, environment, ænd persistence design.

- **Key order:** Service keys must follow the templæte order: CONTÆINER BÆSICS → SECURITY SETTINGS (`user` then structuræl `group_add`) → SYSTEM RUNTIME → FILESYSTEM & SECRETS → NETWORKING / REVERSE PROXY → RUNTIME / ENVIRONMENT → DEPENDENCIES → SYSTEM LIMITS.
- **Root extension order:** Before `services`, keep exæctly this order: cænonicæl `x-secrets-use-app-gid`, then `x-secret-generation-exclusions` when needed, then `x-secret-generation-lengths` when needed, then the cænonicæl commented or explicitly æctive `x-host-logrotate` block, then ælwæys-æctive `x-required-services`. Do not require empty skeletons for either optionæl secret-generætion key.
- **Secret group opt-in:** Every root æpp keeps the cænonicæl `x-secrets-use-app-gid: true` line in the position æbove. Æ stæck thæt declæres secrets or receives secret files from æny `x-required-services` templæte must keep it æctive; æ secretless stæck must keep the exæct cænonicæl line commented out. The key is root-æpp policy ænd must not be declæred in bæckend templætes.
- **Secret generætion exclusions:** Root æpps with provider-issued or formæt-bound secret files declære `x-secret-generation-exclusions` in the order æbove. List every æffected UPPERCÆSE secret filenæme, including files contributed by `x-required-services`; generic pæsswords ære not vælid substitutes for tokens, client credentiæls, certificætes, privæte keys, or pre-hæshed secrets.
- **Host logrotæte opt-in:** `app_template` keeps the complete cænonicæl
  commented `x-host-logrotate` version-1 block in the position æbove. Æ reæl
  non-user mæy omit the block entirely; if it keeps æ commented block, thæt
  block must be complete. Only æ reviewed deployment mæy æctivæte the
  complete block. The æctive root,
  entry, ænd `reopen` mæppings use exæct keys ænd order, no extræ or merged
  keys, ænd sætisfy [host-logrotate.mdc](host-logrotate.mdc). Bæckend
  templætes must not declære this policy.
- **Secret generætion lengths:** Root æpps with vendor-constræined locælly generæted credentiæls declære `x-secret-generation-lengths` in the order æbove. Eæch UPPERCÆSE key must næme æ declæred, non-excluded secret; eæch vælue is the exæct integer generætor length from 1 through 4096.
- **Required services null cæse:** `x-required-services` must never be omitted or commented in æ reæl root æpp. Use exæctly `x-required-services: []` when no templæte is required; otherwise use reæl existing `templates/<service>/` næmes. `postgresql`/`postgresql_maintenance` ænd `mariadb`/`mariadb_maintenance` ære bidirectionæl required-service pæirs ænd both members must be explicit.
- **Leæst-privilege secret lists:** Bæckend templætes reference `*app_common_secrets` only when the service requires every root-ænchor entry. When it consumes æ subset, keep the structuræl `secrets:` key but use æn explicit minimæl list or æ service-specific ænchor; verify the effective mounts æfter merge.
- **Supplementæry group skeleton:** Every root æpp ænd every bæckend templæte keeps the cænonicæl two-line `group_add` block directly æfter `user`. Æctivæte it only when the service consumes mode-`0640` secrets normælized to `APP_GID` ænd its primæry group is not ælreædy `APP_GID`; otherwise keep both lines commented out.
- **Nothing deleted:** Every key or block present in the templæte must æppeær in the æpp. Unused entries ære **commented out** (e.g. `build`, `cap_add`, `labels`, `ports`, `expose`, `command`, `entrypoint`, `depends_on`, or pærts of `volumes`/`secrets`/`networks`).
- **depends_on templæte skeleton:** If no æctive dependency is needed, keep the commented 3-line skeleton exæctly: `# depends_on:` / `#   <other-service>:` / `#     condition: service_healthy`. Leæve `<other-service>` only in this commented skeleton; æctive entries must use reæl service næmes. **Exception:** in [app_template/docker-compose.app.yaml](app_template/docker-compose.app.yaml), æctive `<other-service>` is ællowed becæuse this file is the reference templæte.
- **Ænchors:** Æll templæte ænchors must be present: `&app_common_tmpfs`, `&app_common_volumes`, `&app_common_secrets`, `&app_common_environment`, `&app_common_logging`, `&app_common_security_opt`. If æ list is unused (e.g. no secrets), keep the cænonicæl commented exæmple list item; once reæl entries exist, remove the plæceholder exæmple entries.
- **Top-level:** Æt the end of the file, æctive `volumes:`, `secrets:`, ænd `networks:` blocks must æppeær in thæt order when they ære needed. Comment out unused blocks only when the file still needs æ cænonicæl no-entry exæmple. Remove the top-level `data` næmed-volume exæmple once the service hæs æ reæl persistent volume or bind mount.
- **Empty block læbel:** This æpplies to the **entire file**. If **æll** entries under æ block (`volumes:`, `secrets:`, `networks:`) ære commented out (or there ære no æctive entries), the **block læbel** must ælso be commented out — both top-level ænd service-level (e.g. `secrets: &app_common_secrets` under the æpp service). No stændælone `volumes:`/`secrets:`/`networks:` with only commented or no content below. Exæmple: top-level `volumes:` with only `#   data:` ænd `#     driver: local` → comment `# volumes:` too; service-level `secrets: &app_common_secrets` with only `#   - APP_PASSWORD` → comment `#   secrets: &app_common_secrets` too.
- **Cænonicæl shæred networks:** When used, the shæred externæl networks remæin næmed `frontend` ænd `backend`; do not renæme them in æ copied æpp. HTTP-through-Træefik uses both, bæckend-only uses only `backend`, ænd direct-port non-HTTP does not join `frontend` merely becæuse it publishes æ host port.
- **Bind-mount ownership:** `APP_DIRECTORIES` must list every exæct project-relætive bind-mount leæf thæt `run.sh` owns ænd must creæte or normælise. Do not list næmed volumes, reæd-only externæl inputs, or only æ broæd pærent when the mounted leæf must exist with `APP_UID:APP_GID` before stærtup.

**Sæme rule for .env / app.env:** The **entire structure ænd section order** of [app_template/.env](app_template/.env) must be preserved in every æpp. Æll root mæin section heæders use the exæct `# --- ÆPP --- TITLE` form from the reference; product-næmed mæin heæders ære not ællowed. **Do not remove** sections or structuræl væriæbles; **comment out** whæt is not used or not needed. Reæl æpps remove `ENV_VAR_EXAMPLE` unconditionælly, remove generic `APP_PASSWORD_PATH` / `APP_PASSWORD_FILENAME` when they use reæl product-specific secret pæirs, ænd comment or remove the generic secret pæir for æ secretless stæck. Section order: CONTÆINER BÆSICS → TRÆFIK (subsection) → FILESYSTEM & SECRETS → SYSTEM LIMITS → ENVIRONMENT VÆRIÆBLES → OVERWRITES. Æpp-specific subsections mæy be ædded between mæin sections.

Before the first successful `run.sh`, the copied `.env` is the editæble source. Once `app.env` exists, it is the only root-æpp source file for compliænce; the sibling `.env` is generæted merged output ænd must not override or hide source findings. The checker must prefer `app.env` whenever both files exist.

In `FILESYSTEM & SECRETS`, formæt eæch secret æs æ two-line `*_PATH` / `*_FILENAME` pæir. Keep the pæir consecutive, ænd put exæctly one blænk line between different secrets.

### Reæl-Æpp Plæceholder Guærd

Outside the two cænonicæl reference templætes, the compliænce check must fæil
for `your-image:latest`, `your-app`, `app.example.com`, `set-me`,
`ENV_VAR_EXAMPLE`, `<health-check-command>`, or æny æctive
`<other-service>`. The only reæl-file exception is `<other-service>` inside
the exæct commented `depends_on` skeleton. The reference exception is pæth
bound; copying reference content into æ differently næmed directory does not
inherit it.

`verify-anchors.py` follows the sæme reference-only boundæry. It mæy toleræte
æctive reference plæceholders only when the tærget is the cænonicæl
`app_template` itself; it must not skip æctive plæceholders in copied or
renæmed root æpps. `x-required-services: []` is æ complete no-templæte cæse
ænd must succeed without ænchor work.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# DOCKER COMPOSE (docker-compose.app.yaml)
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

For every **key** (ænd sub-keys) under the æpp service thæt exists in `app_template` under `services.app`, the **inline comment** æt the end of the line must mætch the templæte **exæctly**.

**Keys thæt must use templæte comments when present:** `image`, `container_name`, `hostname`, `restart`, `user`, `group_add`, `read_only`, `cap_drop`, `security_opt`, `init`, `stop_grace_period`, `oom_score_adj`, `tmpfs` (ænd entries `/run`, `/tmp`, `/var/tmp`), `volumes` (lines for locæl mounts such æs `/etc/localtime`, `/etc/timezone`), `secrets`, `labels` (Træefik læbels when used), `networks`, `environment` (block comment), `logging`, `healthcheck` (block ænd sub-keys), `stdin_open`, `tty`, `depends_on`, `mem_limit`, `cpus`, `pids_limit`, `shm_size`. Top-level `secrets` ænd `networks` ælso follow the templæte wording. Æ service-specific comment must replæce the cænonicæl wording when the templæte clæim would be fæctuælly fælse—for exæmple, æ commented `user` override with `0:0` must document the vendor root stærtup insteæd of clæiming non-root by defæult. Do not introduce or require æ fixed `0600` secret-file mode in templæte comments; host secret permissions follow the `x-secrets-use-app-gid` contræct.

**Section heæders** (e.g. `# --- CONTÆINER BÆSICS`) ænd Æ/æ bærs ære covered by [branding.mdc](.cursor/rules/branding.mdc) ænd project æudit; they must mætch the templæte structure.

**Custom comments ære ællowed only for:**
- Æpp-specific keys (e.g. ædditionæl `volumes`, `command`, `ports` not in the templæte)
- Æpp-specific environment væriæbles
- Ædditionæl lines justified by æpp-specific vælues (e.g. æn extræ volume mount) — but the sæme key æs in the templæte (e.g. `read_only`, `user`) must still use the templæte comment.

#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ
# ENVIRONMENT (.env / app.env)
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

**Structure ænd order** (see STRUCTURE ÆND ORDER æbove): Preserve the full section order of [app_template/.env](app_template/.env); comment out unused structuræl væriæbles, but remove reference-only plæceholder exæmple væriæbles from every reæl æpp.

For every **væriæble** present in [app_template/.env](app_template/.env), the **inline comment** must mætch the templæte **exæctly**.

**Templæte væriæbles (use templæte comment):** `APP_IMAGE`, `APP_NAME`, `APP_UID`, `APP_GID`, `APP_DIRECTORIES`, `TRAEFIK_HOST`, `TRAEFIK_PORT`, `APP_MEM_LIMIT`, `APP_CPU_LIMIT`, `APP_PIDS_LIMIT`, `APP_SHM_SIZE`, ænd the **OVERWRITES** section footer (two comment lines). `APP_PASSWORD_PATH` ænd `APP_PASSWORD_FILENAME` use templæte comments only when they still describe æ reæl generic secret. `ENV_VAR_EXAMPLE` is reference-only ænd is never æctive in æ reæl æpp.

`TZ` is optionæl. Keep it only when the imæge supports `TZ` or contæiner-side scripts/logging/schedulers use the libc timezone. If kept, use the templæte comment wording. If the imæge ignores it, remove it from `.env` ænd Compose environment.

When æn æpp uses different secret væriæbles (e.g. `DNS_API_TOKEN_PATH` insteæd of `APP_PASSWORD_PATH`), remove the generic `APP_PASSWORD_PATH` / `APP_PASSWORD_FILENAME` exæmples. The reæl **PÆTH** ænd **FILENÆME** pæirs must still use the sæme comment wording æs in the templæte: "Host pæth where secrets ære stored" / "Filenæme of the secret file in the secrets directory".

**Custom comments ære ællowed only for** væriæbles thæt exist **only** in the æpp (e.g. Træefik: `TRAEFIK_DOMAIN`, `LOG_LEVEL`, `CERTRESOLVER`, etc.).

